course: dictionary
lesson: 2552
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word degree is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, which is its context. «Water freezes at 0 degrees Celsius» is about heat, but «A right angle is 90 degrees» is about angles.
explain: Look for the clues. Words like Celsius, hot, cold, or temperature show that degree means a unit for measuring heat. Words like angle, triangle, or turn show that it means a unit for measuring the size of an angle.
explain: Degree can also mean a qualification from college or university, or «to some degree», which means partly. Always test your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: A degree is a unit for measuring how hot or cold something is.
fact: A degree is also a unit for measuring the size of an angle: a right angle is 90 degrees, a straight line is 180 degrees, and a full turn is 360 degrees.
fact: A degree can be the qualification you get when you finish university, and «to some degree» means partly or a bit.
fact: Temperatures are written with a small circle, like this: 20°.
fact: The same word can mean different things, so context clues help you choose the right meaning.
exercise: «A right angle is 90 degrees.» What does degrees measure in this sentence? | How hot or cold something is | *The size of an angle | How many years someone studied | How heavy something is
exercise: «Normal body temperature is about 36.5 to 37.5 degrees Celsius.» What does degrees Celsius measure? | Angles in a triangle | How much something weighs | How fast something moves | *How hot or cold the body is
exercise: «I agree with you to some degree.» What does «to some degree» mean? | *Partly, a bit | Very loudly | Completely, with no doubt at all | At a steep angle
test: «Mercury's daytime surface reaches about 430 degrees Celsius, hot enough to melt lead.» What does this sentence tell us about degrees? | It measures the size of a corner | It shows how far away Mercury is | It counts the years a planet takes to go round the Sun | *It measures how hot the surface is
test: «Vent water can be hotter than three hundred degrees, but it does not boil because of the huge pressure of the deep sea.» Why does the water not boil? | Because degrees make water safe | It is too cold to boil | Because it has no water in it | *Because of the huge pressure of the deep sea
exam: «Inside the huddle it can be more than 20 degrees warmer than outside.» What does «20 degrees warmer» mean? | It has 20 more penguins than outside | It is 20 kilometres further away | *Its temperature is more than 20 units higher | It turns through an angle of 20 degrees
